We should consider a case of `self.label` is an empty string. In this case, the label string will be ended with a new line, and it looks like a bug. I'd like to suggest some solutions.

```python
if self._diagram.autolabel:
    self.label = :"\n".join(filter(None, [self.__class__.__name__, self.label]))

# or

if self._diagram.autolabel:
    prefix = self.__class__.__name__
    if self.label:
        self.label = prefix + "\n" + self.label
    else:
        self.label = prefix
